[{:adr/consequences "{:addendum_2607071730 {:bug_2_fixed {:what \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#2 (pin advanced): joint-set computation moved\\n           before mesh merge so it can build joint-index-of and rewrite every\\n           skinned mesh's JOINTS_0 data with real remapped values\", :tolerance \"a JOINTS_0 slot referencing an unmappable joint no longer throws\\n               unconditionally -- only when its paired WEIGHTS_0 is genuinely\\n               non-zero; real content commonly leaves harmless arbitrary indices\\n               in zero-weight slots from a whole-file shared skin\", :verification \"two new regression tests with unambiguous right/wrong answers\\n                  (reversed joint order; unmappable+zero-weight vs.\\n                  unmappable+real-weight), both confirmed to distinguish pre-fix\\n                  from post-fix behavior, not just non-crash. 44 tests/158\\n                  assertions\"}, :bug_3_open {:what \"composing the ACTUAL real-world pair (Seed-san base + VRM1_\\n           Constraint_Twist_Sample donor hair) still throws, now on a DIFFERENT\\n           unmappable joint -- a full non-zero weight on a node whose name\\n           resolves to a leg-related bone, implausible for a hair vertex\", :diagnosis_status \"inconclusive this cycle -- an ad-hoc browser probe script\\n                       (hand-rolled cljs.core interop) produced CONTRADICTORY\\n                       results across two attempts about which of the donor's 3\\n                       skins the hair mesh's node actually references, meaning\\n                       the PROBE ITSELF is suspect, not necessarily compose\", :next_step \"add direct in-code diagnostics (a deftest against the actual\\n               Seed-san/VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample bytes) rather than more\\n               hand-rolled browser-script JS interop, so the diagnosis tool is\\n               held to the same rigor as the fixes\", :blocks \"net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped\"}}, :addendum_2607071800 {:method \"a direct clojure -M -e script against the actual downloaded .vrm bytes\\n            (vrm.parse/vrm.part/vrm.compose called directly, JVM ex-data inspected) --\\n            addendum 2's own recommendation, followed this time. Immediately caught\\n            that addendum 2's browser probe had read the WRONG skin (donor has 3\\n            skins; hair mesh uses skin 2; probe inspected skin 0) and reported a\\n            bogus node/bone name as a result\", :bug_4_fixed {:what \"the real unmappable-joint case carries weight 0.00266 (~0.27%), an\\n           ordinary blend-smoothing residual -- addendum 2's 1e-4 tolerance was too\\n           strict for real content\", :fix \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#3 (pin advanced): raised to 1e-2 (1%), with a test\\n         locking in the exact real-world value\"}, :bug_5_confirmed_bigger {:what \"Seed-san has 5 SEPARATE skins, one per mesh (hair=23 joints,\\n           hair_tail=7, head=1, robo_arm=21, wear=80) -- compose's whole design\\n           assumes ONE shared skin per document (base-skin = first skin). A mesh\\n           using any other skin has joints joint-index-of doesn't contain, so even\\n           Seed-san's OWN wear/body mesh fails the unmappable-joint check against\\n           its OWN base document -- not a donor issue at all\", :confidence \"CONFIRMED with certainty this time (not addendum 2's\\n                'inconclusive') -- verified via the reliable direct-JVM method\", :real_fix_scope \"unify a document's own multiple skins into one before donor\\n                     merging, or extend composed output to support multiple skins --\\n                     a genuine architecture decision (likely its own ADR), not a\\n                     bounded patch\", :blocks \"net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped\"}, :lesson \"the previous cycle's unreliable browser-script diagnosis was itself the\\n           obstacle -- switching to direct in-JVM calls against real bytes (no\\n           browser, no JS interop) resolved the ambiguity immediately and is the\\n           right default tool for future org-vrmc-vrm diagnosis\"}, :followups [\"compose->export integration test against a real fixture .vrm (synthetic\\n               docs cover selection/transforms; buffer merge rides the engine's own\\n               116-assertion suite meanwhile)\" \"kotobase-backed SpecStore (:db-api wiring)\" \"the editor app inside babiniku (ADR-2607071600 M6)\" \"expression/texture/spring-bone ops -- engine supports them; additive\"], :addendum_2607071700 {:context \"building net-babiniku's actual cross-avatar part-swap UI (M6 slice 2)\\n             surfaced two real org-vrmc-vrm/vrm.compose bugs, invisible in every prior\\n             compose test/usage because those all composed parts from the SAME source\\n             document\", :bug_1_fixed {:what \"compose's skin rebuild grew a skin's :joints with donor joints but reused\\n           the base's own (shorter) inverseBindMatrices accessor unchanged -- real\\n           avatars threw 'No item N in vector of length N' loading the composed GLB\", :fix \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#1 (pin advanced): build a genuinely new IBM\\n          accessor spanning the grown joint list when growth occurs; regression test\\n          on a synthetic fixture confirmed to fail pre-fix with the same exception\"}, :bug_2_open {:what \"compose's mesh/attribute remap only redirects which ACCESSOR a :JOINTS_0\\n           attribute points to, never remaps the per-vertex joint-index VALUES inside\\n           it -- those stay 'position in the donor's OWN original skin joint array',\\n           wrong once every mesh binds to the ONE unified skin's different joint order.\\n           Symptom: composed avatar loads (bug 1 fixed) but renders visibly distorted\", :real_fix_scope \"reorder compose's phases (joint-set/node-remap must resolve\\n                     BEFORE mesh merge, not after) + component-type-aware\\n                     decode/remap/re-encode of every donor mesh's JOINTS_0 data --\\n                     materially larger and riskier than bug 1, correctly deferred\\n                     rather than attempted blind in the cycle that found it\", :blocks \"net-babiniku M6 slice 2 (cross-avatar part-swap); M6 slice 1 (reuse base\\n             avatar as-is, no cross-document compose) is unaffected and remains\\n             what's shipped\"}, :consequence \"the part-swap UI built this cycle was NOT shipped (reverted, no PR)\\n                rather than ship a visibly broken character -- this ADR's own\\n                fail-loudly invariant applied to itself\"}, :addendum_2607080100 {:context \"addendum 3 deferred the multi-skin question as 'a real architecture\\n             decision, not a bounded patch' -- revisited with a concrete design and\\n             found smaller than expected: the JOINTS_0 remap machinery (bug_2_fixed)\\n             was ALREADY skin-index-agnostic, only joint-set/IBM seeding assumed one\\n             skin per document\", :bug_5_fixed {:what \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#4 (pin advanced): joint-set seeding now unions\\n           EVERY skin any source document (base or donor) actually has, not just\\n           (first (:skins doc)); ibm-plan entries gained :skin-idx so the\\n           inverseBindMatrices build reads each joint's real matrix from whichever\\n           specific skin -- any document, any index -- it actually came from\", :verification \"new regression test mirrors the exact real failure shape (a\\n                   document's SOLE selected mesh using skin index 1, not 0) --\\n                   confirmed to fail pre-fix with the identical error signature as\\n                   the real Seed-san bug, pass with the fix. 46 tests/164 assertions.\\n                   Verified against the real Seed-san file (direct JVM diagnostic):\\n                   composing it as a base no longer fails on its own structure AT\\n                   ALL -- every one of its 5 skins now handled correctly\"}, :bug_6_open_narrower {:what \"composing the full real pair (Seed-san + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample)\\n           still throws, but now on ONE different, precisely identified issue\\n           entirely on the donor side: J_Sec_Hair1_01, a genuine hair-sway\\n           secondary/physics bone with a real 4.1% skinning weight, parented under\\n           J_Bip_C_Head rather than under the hair mesh's own node\", :root_cause \"invisible to vrm.part/decompose's current node-indices heuristic\\n                (walks only the selected mesh's own node subtree) -- a vrm.part\\n                question, not a vrm.compose defect\", :real_question \"should a decomposed part's node-indices also include secondary/\\n                    spring-bone descendants of humanoid-bone ancestors, even when\\n                    they're not descendants of the mesh's own node? -- narrower and\\n                    more concrete than the open-ended 'architecture decision' this\\n                    addendum chain started with\", :blocks \"net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI remains unshipped, but the\\n             blocker is now singular and well-understood, not an open architecture\\n             question\"}}, :addendum_2607080900 {:context \"addendum 5 closed the last engine blocker; this addendum ships the\\n             consumer UI it unblocked -- kisekae.build/kisekae.edit/kisekae.spec\\n             already had a complete, tested API, net-babiniku just never called it\\n             from the create-your-character form\", :shipped {:what \"jk-luxury/net-babiniku#38: swap-parts picker (one row per\\n           kisekae.spec/overridable-kind) wired to kisekae.spec's :op/add-part via\\n           kisekae.edit, compose happens ON DEMAND at stage-select time (not\\n           creation time) via a new babiniku.web/ensure-composed-avatar!, cached\\n           by character-id\", :design_rationale \"the character record stores only the small kisekae.spec\\n                       (base + overrides), not an eagerly-built blob -- matches\\n                       kisekae.spec's own 'not a .vrm file in a bucket' design.\\n                       An eager blob URL would not survive page reload\\n                       (URL.createObjectURL dies with the browsing context) and\\n                       would blow past localStorage's quota for multi-MB avatars\", :perf_note \"the composed VrmDocument feeds straight into\\n               vrmb/load-avatar-meshes, skipping export-bytes + reparse entirely\\n               -- compose already produces a real VrmDocument in memory\"}, :verification {:method \"live browser verification, twice -- NOT a mock, NOT a local dev\\n             server (this session's browser-automation tool runs in a different\\n             network namespace than the sandbox that builds the code, discovered\\n             mid-verification when localhost was unreachable from the browser).\\n             Used a real Cloudflare Pages preview deploy first, then production\\n             itself after merge\", :real_pair \"created a character with Aoi (Seed-san) as base + Yui's\\n               (VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample) hair as an override -- the exact\\n               real-world pair addendum 5 verified via direct JVM diagnostic, now\\n               verified through the full browser UI/engine/render pipeline\", :confirmed \"selecting it on stage showed 'building your character's avatar...'\\n               (proves the compose branch, not plain-fetch, was taken) then\\n               '(triangle) live VRM avatar'; the composed avatar rendered as a\\n               full, correctly-posed, textured humanoid with hair visibly distinct\\n               from Aoi's own short black hair -- confirmed by direct side-by-side\\n               comparison. No console errors. The plain no-override fast path\\n               re-verified unaffected\"}, :bug_caught_before_landing {:what \"the swap-parts picker's .selected CSS class had no matching style rule\\n           (only .base-picker button.selected existed) -- every row looked\\n           unselected even though the underlying re-frame state was correct\", :how_caught \"screenshot inspection during verification, not code review\", :fix \"extended the existing CSS rule to also cover .part-swap-row\\n         button.selected; rebuilt, redeployed, reverified\"}}, :first_consumer \"net-babiniku gains the kisekae dependency at ADR-2607071600 M6\", :addendum_2607080800 {:context \"addendum 4 narrowed the remaining blocker to one precise question:\\n             should a decomposed part's node-indices also include secondary/\\n             spring-bone descendants of humanoid-bone ancestors, even when they're\\n             not descendants of the mesh's own node? -- answered yes, fixed in\\n             vrm.part (decompose defines what a part touches), not vrm.compose\", :bug_7_fixed {:what \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm#5 (pin advanced): decompose now seeds a part's\\n           node-indices with every node the part's own mesh's JOINTS_0 vertex data\\n           genuinely resolves to (decoded the same way\\n           vrm.compose/remap-joints-accessor! does), on top of the existing pure\\n           descendant-walk\", :self_caught_bug \"an earlier draft seeded a whole skin's DECLARED :joints\\n                      palette unconditionally (not just the joints a mesh's own\\n                      vertices actually reference) -- wrong, since a skin is a\\n                      shared glTF object; this over-grew the unified skeleton with\\n                      joints no vertex in that mesh ever binds to. Caught via 5\\n                      real test regressions, diagnosed to the exact mechanism,\\n                      corrected to decode actual per-vertex JOINTS_0 values instead\", :test_premise_updated \"compose-still-throws-on-genuinely-weighted-unmappable-\\n                           joint's old fixture (a joint reachable via neither\\n                           humanoid-mapping nor node-indices) is now legitimately\\n                           resolved by this fix -- correctly so. Redesigned around\\n                           what remains a genuine defect: an out-of-range JOINTS_0\\n                           local-pos with no entry in the skin's own :joints array\\n                           at all (malformed data, not reachability)\", :verification \"new regression test (decompose-seeds-secondary-bone-not-a-\\n                   structural-descendant) reproduces the exact real-world topology\\n                   (secondary bone under Head, sibling to the mesh's own node, ~4%\\n                   weight matching J_Sec_Hair1_01's real ~4.1%) and is confirmed to\\n                   fail pre-fix with the identical error signature as the real bug\\n                   (ExceptionInfo ... no place in the unified skeleton, weight\\n                   0.04). Full suite: 47 tests/169 assertions, 0 failures\"}, :real_world_result {:what \"composing the FULL real Seed-san (base, all 4 of its own decomposed\\n           parts) + VRM1_Constraint_Twist_Sample's real hair as donor now succeeds\\n           end to end -- compose, GLB export, and reparse all complete without\\n           error (1 unified skin, 363 joints, 6 meshes, 424 nodes)\", :method \"re-downloaded both real files fresh from vrm-c/vrm-specification,\\n             direct JVM diagnostic (same established method as addenda 3-4)\", :significance \"the exact real-world avatar pair this addendum chain set out to\\n                   support composes cleanly for the first time -- the compose/\\n                   decompose engine investigation this ADR has tracked across 5\\n                   addenda is now closed\"}, :unblocks \"net-babiniku M6 slice 2 part-swap UI can be revisited on the\\n              strength of an engine proven against real, unmodified Consortium\\n              content, not synthetic fixtures alone\"}, :shipped \"repo scaffolded/pushed/registered (west.yml, this landing commit); 33 checks\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["the VRM character editor lives at kotoba-lang/kisekae as a pure-.cljc DOMAIN library\n    (no UI) over org-vrmc-vrm's existing decompose/compose/export engine -- the editor\n    layer was the missing piece, not the engine" "the character spec (small plain EDN: base URL, part overrides, material edits, user\n    meta) is the artifact of record; the .vrm is deterministically rebuilt from it on\n    demand, never stored as the truth" "dress-up semantics: one override per part kind (replace, not stack); :body is never\n    overridable (the base's skeleton is compose's :skeleton-base); part vocabulary\n    derives from vrm.part/part-categories, never a parallel list" "edits are data ({:op/type ...}), applied by one pure fn; unknown ops / unfetched URLs\n    / missing donor parts THROW -- never silent no-ops or substitutions" "persistence is a SpecStore protocol with MemSpecStore built+tested now, plus the pure\n    kotobase datom mapping (spec->tx/entity->spec, document-as-datom); the kotobase-backed\n    record via the :db-api map is follow-up wiring, not design" "runtime priority honestly applied: interop-free .cljc, cljs-executable today,\n    kototama-subset by construction, zero #?(:kototama) branches (the feature doesn't\n    exist); .kotoba numeric cores are recorded aspiration only" "UI belongs to consumers: canvaskit viewport + kami-webgpu preview + kotoba-lang/editor\n    controls; first app is babiniku.net's create-your-character flow (ADR-2607071600 M6)"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-kisekae", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607071600-net-babiniku-service-completion-design.md" "90-docs/adr/2607071130-kotoba-lang-canvaskit-scroll-view-consolidation.md" "90-docs/adr/2607021330 (kotoba-lang org visibility = public)"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607071610-kotoba-lang-kisekae-vrm-character-editor", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-07", :adr/decision "{:library \"kotoba-lang/kisekae (着せ替え) -- pure .cljc, one dep (org-vrmc-vrm), no UI;\\n            public repo, pushed @ adc47d0, 33-check nbb gate, clj-kondo clean\", :namespaces {:kisekae.spec \"character-spec EDN + problem-list validation + overridable-kinds\\n                  derived from vrm.part/part-categories (minus :body :other) +\\n                  part-urls fetch-list\", :kisekae.edit \"ops (:op/rename :op/set-meta :op/add-part[replace-per-kind]\\n                  :op/remove-part :op/set-base-color), op-log history with undo/redo and\\n                  redo-tail truncation; unknown op throws\", :kisekae.build \"effective-sources (base minus overridden kinds + donor parts,\\n                   :skeleton-base tracked) -> compose -> apply-material-edits\\n                   (baseColorFactor) -> apply-meta (USER's name/authors/license) ->\\n                   export-glb; pure given docs-by-url, caller does I/O; missing anything\\n                   throws\", :kisekae.store \"SpecStore protocol + MemSpecStore (tested), spec->tx/entity->spec pure\\n                   datom mapping ({:kisekae/id :kisekae/name :kisekae/spec-edn},\\n                   document-as-datom) for the future kotobase-backed record via the\\n                   :db-api map\"}, :invariants [\"spec is the artifact; .vrm is derived cache\" \":body never overridable -- skeleton swapping is a rigging problem this editor does\\n     not pretend to solve\" \"fail loudly: no silent op drops, no silent part substitution\" \"license meta is first-class at export; base/donor license compatibility is the\\n    consuming app's concern to surface, not build's to fake-check\"], :runtime_priority \"interop-free .cljc; cljs today; kototama-subset by construction; no\\n                     #?(:kototama); .kotoba aspiration recorded, not claimed\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-07: 'vrm character editor なども kotoba-lang として、\\n           ユーザーが使いやすいものを再設計して. kotoba wasm, cljc, kotobase datomic' --\\n           confirmed 'do it'\", :engine_already_exists {:what \"kotoba-lang/org-vrmc-vrm (restored from the deleted kami-vrm Rust crate,\\n          ADR-2607010930): vrm.part/decompose (parts classified #{:body :hair :face\\n          :outfit :accessory :other}, production-hardened name heuristic),\\n          vrm.compose/compose (cross-document merge onto a unified :skeleton-base),\\n          vrm.export/export-glb (VRM 1.0 GLB out, via kotoba-lang/glb), plus mtoon/\\n          expressions/springs/humanoid and zero-dep JSON+math\", :missing \"everything AROUND the engine: persisted document model of user choices,\\n             pure edit ops + undo/redo, selection logic into compose inputs, storage\\n             contract\"}, :adjacent_blocks \"canvaskit (viewport gestures), editor (walk-EDN controls), webgpu\\n                    (preview), kotobase :db-api (persistence) -- compose, don't rebuild\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"store exported .vrm blobs as the artifact of record\", :rejected_because \"opaque, undiffable, storage-heavy, hostile to kotobase-datomic; the\\n                      rebuild is deterministic so the blob is cache, not truth\"} {:option \"full mesh-modeling editor (VRoid Studio class)\", :rejected_because \"the engine does decompose/compose/recolor, not sculpting --\\n                      claiming otherwise is vaporware; dress-up composition is what the\\n                      engine supports and babiniku needs\"} {:option \"build the editor inside net-babiniku\", :rejected_because \"explicit user direction (kotoba-lang として); private vendor repo is\\n                      the wrong home for a reusable public lib; network-isekai is an\\n                      obvious second consumer\"} {:option \"name it vrm-editor\", :rejected_because \"editor is already the generic EDN-editor lib; Japanese product-name\\n                      family (murakumo/giemon/kenchi/itonami) is the org convention\"} {:option \"wire kotobase persistence now\", :rejected_because \"tested pure mapping makes the follow-up mechanical; blocking a pure\\n                      scaffold on live service wiring couples the wrong things\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607071610: kotoba-lang/kisekae -- VRM character editor as a domain library\n          (spec-as-artifact, org-vrmc-vrm engine, kotobase persistence)"}]